    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0450" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4548</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-11T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 10, 3 p.m. You are instructed to inform President Chamorro that this
                    Government would view with gratification such <pb facs="0451" n="279"
                        xml:id="pg279"/> action on the part of Nicaragua as has been taken by
                    Guatemala. Guatemala’s action was outlined to you in Department’s telegram of
                    May 2, 6 p.m., repeated to you by the Legation at San Salvador.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
